    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "REA McGee are delighted to present 7 Warrenstown Downs, Dublin 15 to the market — a bright and well-proportioned three-bedroom semi-detached home extending to approximately 95 sq. m., with off-street parking to the front and an enclosed rear garden.\r\n\r\nThe property offers a practical layout with generous living accommodation downstairs and three bedrooms upstairs. Presented in neutral tones throughout, the house provides an excellent opportunity for a purchaser to move in and personalise the property over time.\r\n\r\nOn entering the property, a spacious entrance hall provides access to the main living room and staircase to the first floor. The living room is positioned to the front of the house and benefits from two windows providing plenty of natural light. An attractive timber fireplace creates a traditional focal point to the room.\r\n\r\nTo the rear is a bright open-plan kitchen and dining area, a particularly useful everyday living space with direct access to the rear garden through glazed sliding doors. The fitted kitchen incorporates a good range of grey wall and floor units, worktop space, tiled splashback, integrated oven and gas hob, while a window overlooking the garden adds further natural light.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, the accommodation comprises three bedrooms. The generously proportioned primary bedroom spans the rear of the property and benefits from fitted wardrobes and its own en-suite shower room. Two additional bedrooms are positioned to the front.\r\n\r\nA separate main bathroom completes the first-floor accommodation and includes a bath, WC and wash-hand basin.\r\n\r\nOutside, the property benefits from a driveway providing off-street parking together with a lawned area to the front. To the rear is an enclosed garden with a combination of lawn and hard-surfaced patio area, block-built boundary walls and a timber garden shed. The garden offers a useful blank canvas for landscaping, outdoor dining or children's play space."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall / Foyer\r\nApprox. 5.35 m x 2.15 m at its indicated maximum dimensions. A spacious entrance hall with staircase to first-floor accommodation and access to the living room.\r\n\r\nLiving Room — 4.73 m x 3.68 m\r\nBright front-facing reception room with timber flooring, two windows and feature timber fireplace.\r\n\r\nDining Area — 2.97 m x 2.92 m\r\nOpen-plan to the kitchen, with timber flooring and glazed sliding doors providing direct access to the rear garden.\r\n\r\nKitchen — 4.96 m x 2.26 m\r\nFitted kitchen with grey wall and floor units, worktops, tiled splashback, stainless-steel sink, integrated oven and gas hob. Window overlooking the rear garden.\r\n\r\nPrimary Bedroom — 5.24 m x 2.91 m\r\nGenerous double bedroom with timber flooring, two windows and extensive fitted wardrobes.\r\n\r\nEn-Suite — 2.12 m x 1.33 m\r\nWith shower enclosure, WC and wash-hand basin.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 — 3.71 m x 3.00 m\r\nDouble bedroom with timber flooring and front-facing window.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 — 3.71 m x 2.16 m\r\nWell-proportioned third bedroom with timber flooring and front-facing window.\r\n\r\nMain Bathroom — 1.97 m x 1.88 m\r\nWith bath, WC and tiled floor."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Excellent selection of primary and secondary schools nearby\r\nRath Dara Community College approximately 280 m away\r\nSt Patrick’s Senior and Junior Schools within approximately 500–600 m\r\nLadyswell National School approximately 770 m away\r\nConvenient to Blanchardstown Centre\r\nEasy access to the N3 and M50\r\nBus services within a short walk\r\nConvenient to the wider employment, shopping and recreational amenities of Dublin 15\r\nEstablished residential setting with a large green/open space immediately opposite the property"
      },
      {
